{# The local navigation bar of the Proxmox console, on EVERY screen of the area.

   This area is deliberately absent from the application's menus, so this strip is the only way
   from one of its screens to the next: without it each one would be a dead end you leave by
   retyping a URL. The rule it enforces is that every feature must be reachable by clicking from
   /infrastructure - a screen you can only open by knowing its address is a bug here.

   Not .cm-tabs: tabs switch between views of one screen, this moves between screens. `activeNav`
   is the key of the current one, passed by every controller of the area.

   Entries appear as their screens are built; there is deliberately no disabled entry for a screen
   that does not exist yet - a link that goes nowhere teaches nothing. #}
<nav class="cm-localnav" aria-label="{{ 'infrastructureLocalNavLabel'|trans }}">
    <a href="{{ path('app_infrastructure') }}" class="cm-localnav__link{{ activeNav == 'overview' ? ' is-active' }}">{{ 'infrastructureOverviewNavLabel'|trans }}</a>
    <a href="{{ path('app_infrastructure_hosts') }}" class="cm-localnav__link{{ activeNav == 'hosts' ? ' is-active' }}">{{ 'infrastructureHostsNavLabel'|trans }}</a>
</nav>
